## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to implement a real-world cache with per-key TTL, deduplicated async work, and a lightweight pub/sub hook using closures.

## Key Concepts
- Per-key state with closures
- Promise deduplication across concurrent callers
- TTL-based invalidation and manual refresh
- Simple pub/sub for updates without external libs

## Code Example
```javascript
function createNotificationCache(fetchFn, ttlMs) {
  const store = new Map();
  return {
    get(userId) {
      const entry = store.get(userId) || { data: null, inFlight: null, expiry: 0, listeners: [] };
      if (entry.inFlight) return entry.inFlight;
      const p = fetchFn(userId).then(d => {
        entry.data = d;
        entry.expiry = Date.now() + ttlMs;
        entry.inFlight = null;
        return d;
      }).catch(e => { entry.inFlight = null; throw e; });
      entry.inFlight = p;
      store.set(userId, entry);
      return p;
    },
    refresh(userId) {
      const entry = store.get(userId) || { inFlight: null };
      const p = fetchFn(userId).then(d => {
        entry.data = d; entry.expiry = Date.now() + ttlMs; entry.inFlight = null; return d;
      });
      entry.inFlight = p; store.set(userId, entry); return p;
    },
    onUpdate(userId, cb) {
      const entry = store.get(userId) || { listeners: [] };
      entry.listeners.push(cb);
      store.set(userId, entry);
      return () => {
        entry.listeners = entry.listeners.filter(x => x !== cb);
      };
    }
  };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you add automatic re-fetch on update with backoff?
- How would you test concurrency with multiple rapid get(userId) calls?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests mastery of advanced CSS Grid usage, responsive column math, and CSS-only state toggling without JS. It also probes ability to pack variable-height tiles efficiently and to design accessible interactions.

## Key Concepts

- CSS Grid: grid-template-columns, grid-auto-rows: minmax(...), grid-auto-flow: dense

- Responsive design with media queries and CSS variables

- Accessibility: focus-visible, reduced-motion

- CSS-only UI state toggling with data attributes

## Code Example

```css
.grid{ display:grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(6, 1fr); grid-gap: var(--gap,16px); grid-auto-rows: minmax(8rem, auto); grid-auto-flow: dense; }
.grid[data-layout="dense"]{ --gap:8px; --pad:8px; }
.card{ padding: var(--pad,12px); aspect-ratio: 16/9; }
.grid > .card:focus-visible{ outline: 2px solid #5b9bd5; transform: translateY(-2px); }
@media (max-width: 1200px){ .grid{ grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); } }
@media (max-width: 800px){ .grid{ grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce){ .grid, .grid > *{ transition: none; } }
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you scale this to 100+ tiles with dynamic content loading while keeping layout stable?
- How would you adapt for dark mode and ensure accessible color contrast?

## Why This Is Asked
Demonstrates architectural thinking for a reusable timeline with CSS Grid and no JS for layout, while enforcing accessibility and motion constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Grid with alternating placement for left/right alignment
- Central timeline line via pseudo-element
- Animation timing with per-item delays
- Responsive switch to single column; prefers-reduced-motion

## Code Example
```javascript
/* CSS sketch for timeline grid and item styles */
.timeline{ display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr auto 1fr; gap: 1rem;}
.timeline > .item{ display:flex; align-items:center; padding:1rem; }
.timeline > .item:nth-child(odd){ grid-column:1 / 2; justify-content:flex-end; }
.timeline > .item:nth-child(even){ grid-column:3 / 4; justify-content:flex-start; }
.timeline:before{ content:''; grid-column:2; width:2px; background:#bbb; align-self:stretch; }
@media (max-width: 800px){ .timeline{ grid-template-columns:1fr; } .timeline:before{ display:none; } }
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would accessibility be affected if the timeline contained long content?
- How would you adapt for dynamic data loading with CSS only?

